$ HA144A — FULL-SPAN sbeam version (parity cross-check for AE1)
$ Ref: MSC Nastran 2021.3 Aeroelastic Analysis User's Guide, Listing 7-1
$
$ Purpose: an explicit full-span model — NO symmetry doubling — built as an
$ EXACT 2x mirror of the half-span ha144a_sbeam.bdf:
$   * both wings + both canards modelled explicitly (SYMXZ=0)
$   * fuselage centreline CONM2 masses DOUBLED, wing masses MIRRORED, so the
$     full model is a precise 2x replica: same CL (W/S), same CG_x (=17.18 ft).
$ By symmetry it MUST trim to the SAME ANGLEA/ELEV as the half-span (and as
$ NASTRAN Listing 7-2: ANGLEA=0.169191, ELEV=0.492457). Total weight = 16000 lb
$ (= 2 x 8000); trimmed lift must equal 16000 lb with parity=0 (sym=1).
$
$ Units: ft, lb, slug, s
$
SOL 144
TITLE = HA144A sbeam full-span
SUBCASE 1
  TRIM   = 1
  SPC    = 1
SUBCASE 2
  TRIM   = 2
  SPC    = 1
BEGIN BULK
$
